  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{lll}2 & a & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & b\\end{array}\\right]$. If $A^3=4 A^2-A-21 I$, where $I$ is the identity matrix of order $3 \\times 3$, then $2 a+3 b$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
